{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5hRTuyCL63kgux8ssMW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Conventions this repository has:**\n1. Controllers contain business logic directly; there is no service layer (see OrderController:17-46).\n2. Error handling uses exception-driven flow: `ConflictException` (409), `ResourceNotFoundException` (404), thrown from controllers.\n3. Each exception carries an `ErrorCode` enum value for machine-readable identification (ApiExceptions.kt:1-31).\n4. A central `GlobalExceptionHandler` (GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:14-28) converts all `ApiException` to the standard `ApiError` envelope format.\n5. Tests use `MockMvc` with `Spring Boot test context`, checking both HTTP status and `jsonPath(\"$.error.code\")` patterns (ShipmentControllerTest.kt:50-56).\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — must add POST endpoint for confirm; cannot be avoided as it's the new feature.\n2. `ApiError.kt` (ErrorCode enum) — must add a new error code for \"shipment in invalid state for confirmation\" (409 case); required by the error response consistency requirement.\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — must add tests for all four confirm cases (success on CREATED, idempotence on CONFIRMED, 409 on CANCELLED, 404 on missing); required by acceptance criteria #5.\n\n**Risks:**\n1. Modifying the `ErrorCode` enum is noted in the code as \"part of the public API: add one deliberately, never rename one casually\" (ApiError.kt:29). I will add a new code carefully to avoid breaking clients.\n2. The idempotence requirement (\"Confirming a shipment that is already CONFIRMED succeeds and changes nothing\") must be implemented correctly to avoid treating a repeat call as an error.\n\n**Open questions:**\nNone. The ticket clearly specifies all four cases and their HTTP statuses.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add a new method annotated with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")`. It will:\n   - Accept a shipment ID as a path variable.\n   - Call `repository.findById()` and throw `ResourceNotFoundException` with `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` if not found (404).\n   - If the shipment is `CREATED`, update it to `CONFIRMED`, save it, and return `ResponseEntity.ok(updated)`.\n   - If the shipment is `CONFIRMED`, return it unchanged with `ResponseEntity.ok(shipment)` (idempotent).\n   - If the shipment is `CANCELLED`, throw `ConflictException` with a new `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED` error code (409).\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** (ErrorCode enum) — Add a single new enum value: `SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED`. This signals that a shipment in `CANCELLED` status cannot transition to `CONFIRMED`.\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment to CONFIRMED` — POST confirm on CREATED, expect 200 and status=CONFIRMED.\n   - `confirm is idempotent on already confirmed shipment` — POST confirm on CONFIRMED twice, both succeed with 200.\n   - `rejects confirm of a cancelled shipment with 409` — Write CANCELLED shipment directly to repo, POST confirm, expect 409 with error.code=SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED.\n   - `rejects confirm of unknown shipment with 404` — POST confirm on non-existent ID, expect 404 with error.code=SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND.\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- **Use a service class:** I considered extracting business logic to a `ShipmentService`, but the existing architecture (OrderController, ShipmentController) places logic in controllers and this would break consistency. Rejected.\n- **Reuse existing error code (e.g., VALIDATION_FAILED):** This would obscure the reason: VALIDATION_FAILED is for malformed input, not state conflicts. The requirement specifies \"Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API,\" which means using the right error code for the case, as the existing code does. Rejected.\n- **Use HTTP 400 instead of 409 for CANCELLED:** HTTP 400 is for malformed requests; 409 Conflict is semantically correct for \"resource exists but in incompatible state.\" The ticket specifies 409. Not an alternative.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Logic | Write | Return |\n|------|-------|-------|-------|--------|\n| Create → Confirm | shipmentId | find(id) → not found | none | 404 ResourceNotFoundException |\n| Create → Confirm | shipmentId | find(id) → found, CREATED | save(CONFIRMED) | 200 Shipment with status=CONFIRMED |\n| Confirm → Confirm (idempotent) | shipmentId | find(id) → found, CONFIRMED | none | 200 Shipment (unchanged) |\n| Confirm CANCELLED | shipmentId | find(id) → found, CANCELLED | none | 409 ConflictException w/ SHIPMENT_CANNOT_BE_CONFIRMED |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- `test_confirms_created_shipment` — Covers: CREATED → CONFIRMED transition, 200 response, persistence.\n- `test_confirm_is_idempotent` — Covers: CONFIRMED → CONFIRMED (no change), 200 response, retry-safe.\n- `test_confirm_cancelled_shipment_rejected` — Covers: CANCELLED state block, 409 response, correct error code.\n- `test_confirm_unknown_shipment_rejected` — Covers: 404 response, correct error code.\n- Existing tests must keep passing (create, get, list, list order).\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll write the code based on the design."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":736,"cache_read_input_tokens":17628,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":736},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59bc1b5f-0053-4ecb-b42c-57f9d5efaba8","uuid":"5cdef1c4-5370-4c7f-b178-0b07fe23c1a2","timestamp":"2026-09-15T18:28:15.419Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5hRTCZ6qzYAZFjcGyXZ"}
